H='（聽力稿，原題播放兩次）\n'
P='（聽力稿）選出最適合的回應：\n'
PIC='\n請選出符合描述的圖片。'
PS=[]
D=[
(1,H+'There is no fruit in the basket. Only a watermelon is next to it.'+PIC,['圖(A)','圖(B)','圖(C)'],[('el-02',190,650,1225,930)]),
(2,H+'Nancy felt terrible after she saw a ghost movie.'+PIC,['圖(A)','圖(B)','圖(C)'],[('el-02',190,980,1225,1260)]),
(3,H+'All the cars stopped to wait for an old man to cross the road.'+PIC,['圖(A)','圖(B)','圖(C)'],[('el-02',190,1305,1225,1585)]),
(4,P+'My father is a writer. How about yours?',['He loves reading books.','He works in a shoe factory.','He usually goes jogging.'],[]),
(5,P+'How long can I use the computer?',['You can use it once a week.','I bought the computer two months ago.','Thirty minutes. Some people are still waiting.'],[]),
(6,P+'The pink dress looks great on you. How much did you spend on it?',['On the Internet.','I like pink very much.','About one thousand NT dollars.'],[]),
(7,P+'I saw Miss Holt talk to Jake angrily just now.',['What did he do this time?','He had a sore throat.','He always studies hard.'],[]),
(8,P+'Lisa, we are going to Betty’s birthday party. Do you want to join us?',['Betty’s birthday party was great.','Sure. I can’t wait to give Betty a surprise!','No worries. The birthday cake tasted delicious.'],[]),
(9,P+'Mike Lee is my favorite singer. His songs always make me happy.',['Really? The song is great.','Be happy. You can sing, too.','Me too. I love his songs.'],[]),
(10,P+'Look! The cloud in the sky looks like a bear.',['No, it is windy today.','Yeah. It’s so cute.','No way! It won’t rain.'],[]),
(11,P+'Is there anything wrong in the kitchen? I smell something terrible from it.',['Yeah. I burned the chicken.','That’s right. Mom is good at cooking.','Sure. We have enough food.'],[]),
(12,H+'M: Hey, Amy. What are you doing?\nW: I am reading a book about baking. I borrowed it from the library.\nM: Why?\nW: I want to make my cake taste as yummy as the ones in the bakery on the corner.\nM: Wow, it’s not that easy. May I have the pleasure to taste your delicious cake?\nW: No problem. I am going to bake a chocolate cake this afternoon. Come to my place and you can help me with it.\nM: Sure. I can’t wait! See you then.\nW: See you.\nQ: Where is the man going this afternoon?',['To Amy’s house.','To a library.','To a bakery.'],[]),
(13,H+'G: Jason, come here! I know the answer.\nB: Let me see. Oh, your answer is wrong.\nG: What? It’s not possible.\nB: You should do this... and that... See? My answer is right.\nG: No, you are wrong. You miss this part. It is very important!\nB: It is NOT!\nG: Come on! It’s no use fighting here. Let’s go ask Mr. Wang.\nB: Fine! I’m pretty sure he will say my answer is right!\nQ: What are they going to do next?',['Take a quick test.','Find the missing part.','Check the answer with the teacher.'],[]),
(14,H+'M: What are you holding in your hand, Alice?\nW: Two bottles of milk tea.\nM: That’s strange. You always say “No” to drinks.\nW: Don’t worry. The milk tea is sugar free. By the way, some drinks at Rosa’s Milk Tea Shop are on sale.\nM: Oh, I see.\nW: Here. One bottle is for me. The other is for you.\nM: Really? That’s great. I love milk tea. Thanks a lot.\nW: You are welcome.\nQ: How did the man feel when the woman got him a bottle of milk tea?',['Happy.','Angry.','Worried.'],[]),
(15,H+'M: Why didn’t she write a letter back to me? Why not?\nW: Who didn’t write a letter back to you?\nM: Tina. Last week, I sent her a Teddy Bear with a card. In the card, I told her how much I like her, and I hope she can write back to me by this Sunday.\nW: Oh, come on. Sunday is still three days away. Give her some time, OK? By the way, I guess she likes you, too.\nM: Really? Why?\nW: Yes. To be honest, Tina wanted me to go pick up a card with her yesterday. I think the card is for you.\nM: You think so?\nW: Yes. Let’s just wait and see.\nQ: What is the man worried about?',['Tina may not like the Teddy Bear.','Tina probably doesn’t like him.','Tina and the woman won’t be friends.'],[]),
(16,H+'W: I am so excited. My favorite writer, Andy Wu, is coming to Taiwan.\nM: Really? One of his books, Wonderland, is popular with teenagers.\nW: Yeah. I love it, too. He is going to meet his fans in Taipei.\nM: Wow, I can’t wait to see him. Maybe we can go together.\nW: Sure. But first... we have to get the tickets.\nM: How can we get the tickets?\nW: That’s easy. We have to buy his latest book, Happy Island. Each book comes with a free ticket.\nM: Then let’s go to the bookstore now.\nW: Let’s go.\nQ: Why are the man and the woman going to buy Happy Island?',['It is popular with teenagers in Taiwan.','They want to get the tickets to meet the writer.','They like the book by Andy Wu very much.'],[]),
(17,H+'（人群喧鬧聲）\nW: Well, how do you like this night market?\nM: It is not big but has everything! Nice food, cold drinks, clothes and game stands. Everything!\nW: That’s true. It is one of my favorite night markets.\nM: Actually, I was today years old when I learned I was wrong about night markets in Taiwan.\nW: Really? You never tried visiting any one before? But you have been in Taiwan for two years.\nM: I thought there was nothing special about night markets. But now I know it is fun to visit night markets.\nW: Haha, I’m glad you like it.\nQ: When the man says “I was today years old when I learned I was wrong about night markets in Taiwan,” what does he mean?',['He always enjoys the food at the night market.','He will buy a lot of things at the night market.','He never knew it is fun to visit a night market in Taiwan.'],[]),
(18,H+'B: Did you see John’s cellphone?\nG: Yes. I saw that after school yesterday. It is the latest cellphone and it’s very expensive.\nB: That’s right. It’s not cheap for both of us, but forty thousand NT dollars is just a piece of cake for John.\nG: I agree. Do you know that? John’s mother gives him four thousand NT dollars as his pocket money every week.\nB: Oh my! That’s ten times my pocket money! For John about money: easy come, easy go.\nG: That’s true. I think I need a rich mother like John’s.\nQ: What does the boy think about John?',['John likes his mother very much.','John has a lot of pocket money.','John doesn’t like his old cellphone.'],[]),
(19,H+'M: Today is Saturday. Mr. and Mrs. Lin don’t have to go to work. Their son and daughter are at home, too. Mr. Lin and his son, Jimmy, are washing the car in the yard. Mrs. Lin is watering the flowers in the garden. Jimmy’s younger sister, Tina, is drawing pictures in the living room. Later, they will go to the restaurant for lunch and see a movie in the afternoon.\nQ: Who is inside the house?',['Tina.','Jimmy.','Mrs. Lin.'],[]),
(20,H+'（廣播聲）\nM: Good morning, everyone. Today is Joy Department Store’s 10th birthday. If you have our Joy Card, check your card number. If it has the number one or zero, show your Joy Card and you can get a free ice cream at Linda’s Kitchen on the third floor. More luckily, if the last two numbers are one and zero, you can enjoy a free meal at John’s Steakhouse on the fifth floor. To celebrate Joy Department Store’s birthday, we prepare 100 Teddy Bears. Go to the top floor with your kid and say “Happy birthday to Joy Department Store,” and your kid can get a Teddy Bear for free.\nQ: If your Joy Card number is 24610, what can you get from Joy Department Store at most?',['An ice cream.','A Teddy Bear.','A meal at John’s.'],[]),
(21,H+'W: OK, are you ready? Please stand in front of that wall. Hey, take it easy. Give me a smile. Good! Now please touch your right shoulder with your right hand and stand like this. And look that way. Oh, don’t forget your smile. Great! You are like a superstar. Now please come here. All your photos are on the computer. Please choose your favorite one.\nQ: What are they doing?',['圖(A)','圖(B)','圖(C)'],[('el-04',190,1480,1225,1755)]),
]
